  "about": "The private tier, version 2 (Sync-API). base = PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256(utf8(secret), salt = utf8(syncSalt), iterations, 32 bytes), as in version 1. key = HKDF-SHA256(ikm = base, salt = keyShare bytes (base64 here, as the server hands it out), info = utf8(\"harvest/sync-key/v2\"), 32 bytes). Envelope {v: 2, iv, ct}: AES-256-GCM, 12-byte IV, 128-bit tag appended to ct, standard base64. A row's additional data is utf8(\"row/<table>/<uuid>/<updatedAt micros>/<deletedAt micros or empty>\"), the micros being instantMicros of the record's clocks, so any spelling of the same instant gives the same aad. After opening, the row's own updatedAt/deletedAt, where its table has those columns, must be the same instants as the record's. Files: aad utf8(\"file/<sha256>\") with this key. keyCheck seals utf8(\"harvest-key-check\") with aad utf8(\"key-check\"). Every case in refused must fail to open. PIN proof (for POST /v1/me/sync-key/unlock): proof = HKDF-SHA256(ikm = base, salt = empty, info = utf8(\"harvest/sync-pin-proof/v1\"), 32 bytes), sent base64; the server keeps verifier = hex(SHA-256(proof)), never the proof. The proofs cases pin it for other secrets and iteration counts.",
